<%# **A trail needs somewhere to go back to.** On a top-level index this rendered "Dashboard > Classrooms"
    directly above an h1 reading "Classrooms" - the page's own name twice, 30px apart - and its one link
    duplicated the sidebar's own Dashboard item. Reported as pushing the content down for no value, and
    measured: 44px of it, taking the h1 from y=128 to y=172 on a 768px viewport.

    Carbon says it outright ("do not use breadcrumbs when there is only one level"), GOV.UK shows the path
    *above* the current page so a top-level page has none, and Polaris has no trail at all - a single back
    action on pages that have a parent. A record page keeps its trail, because "Dashboard > Students > Sam
    Student" has a Students to return to.

    **`shared/`, not `admin/shared/`, because both halves render it.** It lived under admin and the app half
    had no trail at all, which is how `portfolios#show` came to be a page an admin could reach from a record
    and not leave. The root crumb is the only thing that differed - Dashboard for admin, Home for the app -
    so it is a local, and `admin_breadcrumbs` / `page_breadcrumbs` are the two callers that set it.

    Locals:
      breadcrumbs - array of { label:, path: }, the last being the page itself
      root_label  - the first crumb's text
      root_path_for_trail - where the first crumb goes. Not `root_path`: that is a route helper,
                            and a local of the same name shadows it for the whole partial. %>
<% return if breadcrumbs.size < 2 %>

<nav class="flex mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <%# flex-wrap, not inline-flex. As a single unwrappable line the trail pushed <main> sideways on
      six admin pages - a school year's crumb reads "School name (2024-2025)" and took the page
      130px past the viewport at 375px, which carried the row actions off screen with it. gap-x
      matches the old space-x at one line, and gap-y spaces the wrapped rows. %>
  <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1 gap-y-1 lg:gap-x-3">
    <li class="inline-flex items-center">
      <%# **A named focus outline on both links.** They had none, so a keyboard reader got Chrome's default
          1px auto ring - design.md asks for a 2px outline in a named colour, and an unnamed one falls back
          to `currentColor`. It went unnoticed while this partial lived under `admin/`, because the focus
          audit walks the app half's forms; the first app page to render a trail failed it. Fixing it here
          fixes both halves at once, which is the reason the partial moved. %>
      <%# **No icon, on any crumb.** The root carried a house glyph and the rest carried none, which was
          reported as inconsistent, and it is: nothing distinguishes the first crumb except that it is
          first, which the position already says.

          The field is near-unanimous that a trail is plain text - GOV.UK, Carbon, Primer, Bootstrap and
          Atlassian all ship one with no icons, and Polaris has no trail at all. The one common exception is
          Tailwind UI, whose example puts a house on the first item *instead of* a word, as a compact home
          affordance; this had the icon **and** the word, which is that pattern's decoration without its
          economy. Two roots also make the glyph inaccurate - it reads "Dashboard" on the admin half. %>
      <%= link_to root_label, root_path_for_trail,
                  class: "text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:text-sitf-primary-dark " \
                         "focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                         "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" %>
    </li>

    <% breadcrumbs.each_with_index do |crumb, index| %>
      <li>
        <div class="flex items-center">
          <%= lucide_icon("chevron-right", class: "w-3 h-3 text-slate-500 mx-1 shrink-0") %>
          <% if index == breadcrumbs.length - 1 %>
            <span class="ml-1 text-sm font-medium break-words text-slate-500 lg:ml-2">
              <%= crumb[:label] %>
            </span>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to crumb[:label], crumb[:path], class: "ml-1 text-sm font-medium break-words text-slate-700 hover:text-sitf-primary-dark lg:ml-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
</nav>
